      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "40. Why are those suggestive glances, O young women,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "darted from your sportively half-closed ( eyes )? Desist",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "oh desist; vain is this effort ( of yours ). Now changed beings",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "are we; youth is gone; our yearninig ( is only ) for the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "farthest part of a forest; infatuation has subsided; and we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "look upon the meshes of the world as straw.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "41. This young woman constantly darts towards me her",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "eye that steals the beauty of the blue lotus-leaf. What is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "designed by her? Our infatuation is gone; the feverish",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "flame produced by the striking of the flowery arrows",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of the God of Love has been blown out; and yet the poor",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "girl persists !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "42. Why do you, oh God of Love, trouble your hand",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "with the twangings of your bow? Why do you, oh cuckoo,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "chatter ineffectually with your soft and sweet notes? Oh",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "young woman, enough of your glances, affectionate, artful,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "charming, sweet and unsteady; our heart has tasted the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "nectar-like contemplation of the feet of the moon-crested God.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "43. If you do not want to be engulfed in the ocean of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "worldly existence, then leave at a distance this river in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the form of a woman, having about ( the banks ) cruel mon-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "sters in the shape of cruel thoughts, encircled by the waves of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the three furrows on the belly, having a pair of chakrawâka",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "birds on their wing in the form of two high and plump",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "breasts, and decked with a lotus in the shape of the face.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "44. By the five senses, clever in ministering to their own",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "advantage, which have marred supreme bliss, have I been",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "duped being revolved ( in their objects ) thus—Here is melo-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "dious music, here a dance, these are sweet-flavoured viands,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "here is a spreading perfume, and here the touch of breasts.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
